373
01:33:12.761 --> 01:33:37.930
9. Our taxonomy builds on a long tradition in labor economics and occupational analysis. The predecessor to ONET, the Dictionary of Occupational Titles, categorized jobs by “Data/People/Things.” See Fine (1955), Fine and Wiley (1971), Autor and others (2003), Acemoglu and Autor (2011), and Deming (2017).

374
01:33:38.170 --> 01:33:49.733
